# Self-review after code

After any substantive edit (new behavior, multi-file, UI, SRS, worker, or store), do not stop at the first write. Re-check before saying done.

## Always (same turn)

1. Re-read the diff and every call site you touched.
2. Match project rules: no code comments, existing stores/tokens/patterns, AGENTS.md map. If the diff touches UI, also check `.cursor/rules/type-and-icons.mdc` (icon color, title size/color, subtitle size/color).
3. Fix what you find yourself (compile breaks, missing bindings, wrong empty states, leftover comments).
4. Prefer `ReadLints` on edited files when the tool is available.

## When to spawn another agent

Launch a review pass with Task (`generalPurpose` or `explore`) when any of these is true:

- 3+ files changed, or a behavior/product-map change
- Touching SRS, WordsStore, worker prompts, IAP/limits, or notifications
- You are unsure the change is correct end-to-end

Prompt the reviewer with: absolute repo path, files changed, intended behavior, and “find bugs, rule violations, and missed call sites; do not rewrite unless broken.”

Use `bugbot` / security-review **only** when the user explicitly asks for that review.

## Done bar

Only finish after the self-check (and the extra agent, if launched) with no known open issues — or report the leftover risk in one short line.
